From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Make IPL injection reachable on stock builds

INTF.IPL is how an external interrupt controller hands the CPU a level --
the interface PiStorm itself uses. On a stock build, writing it has no
effect: the arbitration accepts the field only through a branch whose level
source, GetIPLLevel(), is a `return 0` stub outside PISTORM_CLASSIC. The
field opens the `if` and the level is then discarded.

That is the same shape as the interrupt registers before this series
existed: the machinery is all present, and one variant holds the only key.

A standalone build wants the PiStorm32 branch, not the classic one, and for
the same reason PiStorm32 does: INTF.IPL already holds a level decided by
something else, so there is nothing to fetch. Here that something else is
Emu68's own core-0 IRQ path rather than Paula over the IPL lines.

This is inert on its own -- nothing writes INTF.IPL on a standalone build
yet. It is the step that makes writing it mean something.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ExecutionLoop.c | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ExecutionLoop.c b/src/ExecutionLoop.c
index f968d72..5caefed 100644
--- a/src/ExecutionLoop.c
+++ b/src/ExecutionLoop.c
@@ -348,8 +348,23 @@ void MainLoop()
                 }
 
                 /* Now, if Higher-level interrupt was coming from Paula, report it */
-#if defined(PISTORM)
-                /* On PiStorm32 IPL level is obtained by second CPU core from the GPIO directly */
+#if defined(PISTORM) || !defined(PISTORM_ANY_MODEL)
+                /*
+                 * On PiStorm32 IPL level is obtained by second CPU core from the GPIO directly.
+                 *
+                 * A standalone build takes the same branch, and for the same
+                 * reason: INTF.IPL is written by something that has already
+                 * decided the level. On PiStorm that is Paula over the IPL
+                 * lines; here it is Emu68's own core-0 IRQ path. Either way the
+                 * field already holds a level and there is nothing to fetch.
+                 *
+                 * The #else below is the PISTORM_CLASSIC path, which reads the
+                 * level from a status register through GetIPLLevel(). That
+                 * function is a `return 0` stub on any other build, so a
+                 * standalone build landing there would open the `if` and then
+                 * discard the level -- which is exactly what made INTF.IPL
+                 * unusable outside PiStorm.
+                 */
                 if (ctx->INTF.IPL > level)
                 {
                     level = ctx->INTF.IPL;
@@ -428,6 +443,28 @@ void MainLoop()
                 /* Set SR */
                 setSR(SR);
 
+#if !defined(PISTORM_ANY_MODEL)
+                /*
+                 * The level has been consumed, so drop it.
+                 *
+                 * On PiStorm INTF.IPL mirrors a physical line that Paula holds
+                 * until the guest acknowledges, so clearing it here would be
+                 * wrong -- hence the guard. Standalone there is no line and no
+                 * Paula: the field is written by Emu68's own core-0 IRQ path,
+                 * once per host interrupt, and nothing else would ever lower
+                 * it. Leaving it set would re-fire the moment the guest's RTE
+                 * drops the SR mask, forever.
+                 *
+                 * Only when the level being taken is the one IPL asked for --
+                 * a higher-priority source (ARM_err at 7) must not swallow a
+                 * pending IPL.
+                 */
+                if (ctx->INTF.IPL && level == ctx->INTF.IPL)
+                {
+                    ctx->INTF.IPL = 0;
+                }
+#endif
+
                 /* Get VBR */
                 vbr = ctx->VBR;
 
